  "name": "Gajdošská kultúra (Slovak gajdy bagpipe music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Bagpipe tradition of Slovakia, inscribed by UNESCO in 2015, built on the gajdy, a goatskin bagpipe with a double chanter that sounds both melody and an accompanying pitch and a separate long drone, its stock often carved as a goat's head. Strongest in central and northern regions such as Liptov, Orava and Horehronie, the gajdoš played alone for song and dance or with fiddles, and the instrument's making and repertoire are handed on from master to pupil and through festivals. The gajda card stands in for the gajdy.",
  "recipe": "classic mid-2010s gajdošská kultúra, drone Modal, wind pipe branch. single reed drone foundation dance accompaniment gajda, fiddle. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
